BUILD ORDER

Build order (so you always have something running)

models.py + Alembic migration → table exists
crud.py functions, tested directly (no LLM yet) — insert, query, sum, update/delete against a scratch SQLite file
tools.py — wrap crud functions as LangChain tools, sanity-check schemas
graph.py + prompts.py — wire up the loop
main.py — manual test script, feed it real message examples (clean, ambiguous, multi-item, income) and check behavior against the policy
Once satisfied → Telegram bot as the input layer, web dashboard as the second client, both calling the same graph

finance-agent/
├── app/
│   ├── db/
│   │   ├── models.py          # SQLAlchemy models
│   │   ├── session.py         # async engine/session
│   │   └── crud.py            # raw DB functions the tools call
│   ├── agent/
│   │   ├── tools.py           # LangChain @tool-decorated functions
│   │   ├── state.py           # AgentState TypedDict
│   │   ├── graph.py           # StateGraph definition
│   │   └── prompts.py         # system prompt
│   ├── config.py              # model name, API keys, constants
│   └── main.py                # test entrypoint (calls the graph directly)
├── alembic/
├── tests/
│   └── test_agent.py          # scripted conversation tests
├── .env
└── requirements.txt

STATE SCHEMA

class AgentState(TypedDict):
    messages: Annotated[list, add_messages]
    user_id: str

TRANSACTIONS SCHEMA

